      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this mapping may legitimately fail with -ENOMEM, we\u0027d better clean up after this failure, i.e. unmap whatever pages we\u0027ve mapped in the hyp MMU and restore the host\u0027s ownership/access to these pages.\n\n...Also while we\u0027re at it, we can improve `pkvm_host_donate_guest()` and `pkvm_host_share_guest()` to check if there are enough pages in the memcache to avoid failing with -ENOMEM in the middle, similarly to the recent improvement in pKVM-ARM: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260501112149.2824881-6-tabba@google.com/. We might leverage our recently added `need_memcache_topup()` for that.",
